window.META_MATH = {"subject": "Representation Theory and Lie Theory", "projects": [{"id": "RT-01", "slug": "maschke-theorem", "title": "Maschke’s Complete Reducibility Theorem", "level": "Introductory", "idea": "<p>An arbitrary projection need not respect the group action. Averaging\nits conjugates creates a projection that does.</p>", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe a finite group,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>\na field in which\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|G|</annotation></semantics></math>\nis invertible, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\na finite-dimensional\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>-representation.\nEvery invariant subspace\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas an invariant complement, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a direct sum of irreducible representations. A representation is a\nhomomorphism\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho:G\\to\\mathrm{GL}(V)</annotation></semantics></math>;\nirreducible means nonzero with no proper nonzero invariant subspace.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Use finite-dimensional basis extension to choose a linear projection\nonto a subspace, invariance under reindexing a finite group sum, and\ninduction on dimension. The field may have positive characteristic\nprovided it does not divide\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|G|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Average a projection", "role": "<p>Average\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho(g)p\\rho(g)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nto enforce equivariance without losing the restriction to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>.\n<strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P=|G|^{-1}\\sum_g\\rho(g)p\\rho(g)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis equivariant, has image\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand restricts to the identity on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>An invariant\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W\\subset V</annotation></semantics></math>\nand any linear projection\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p:V\\to W</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p|_W=\\mathrm{id}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P=|G|^{-1}\\sum_g\\rho(g)p\\rho(g)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis equivariant, has image\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand restricts to the identity on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>Division by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|G|</annotation></semantics></math>\nmust be legal, and each conjugate must still land in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "repair": "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math>\nis assumed equivariant from basis extension alone, replace it by the\nconjugation average and verify the reindexing. Withhold this export and\nrecheck its descendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Choose a vector-space complement by extending a basis of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe its projection. Each conjugate of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math>\nlands in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis invariant under every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho(g)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nOn\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w\\in W</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthat conjugate sends\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w</annotation></semantics></math>\nto itself. Thus the average\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math>\nalso maps into\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>\nand is the identity there.</p>", "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h\\in G</annotation></semantics></math>,\nconjugating\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math>\nby\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho(h)</annotation></semantics></math>\nreplaces the index\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g</annotation></semantics></math>\nby\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">hg</annotation></semantics></math>,\na permutation of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTherefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math>\ncommutes with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho(h)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIts restriction to its image is the identity, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P^2=P</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{im}P=W</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P=|G|^{-1}\\sum_g\\rho(g)p\\rho(g)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis equivariant, has image\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand restricts to the identity on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>An invariant\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W\\subset V</annotation></semantics></math>\nand any linear projection\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p:V\\to W</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p|_W=\\mathrm{id}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Average\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho(g)p\\rho(g)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nto enforce equivariance without losing the restriction to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Division by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|G|</annotation></semantics></math>\nmust be legal, and each conjugate must still land in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Split and terminate", "role": "<p>Use the equivariant kernel as a complement, then induct on dimension.\n<strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V=W\\oplus\\ker P</annotation></semantics></math>\nas representations, and every such\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a finite direct sum of irreducibles.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1 and finite\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dim V</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V=W\\oplus\\ker P</annotation></semantics></math>\nas representations, and every such\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a finite direct sum of irreducibles.</p>", "gate": "<p>The recursive decomposition terminates because each proper nonzero\nsummand has smaller dimension.</p>", "repair": "<p>If repeated splitting is asserted to terminate without a measure, use\nthe strictly decreasing dimensions of the summands. Withhold this export\nand recheck its descendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math>\ndecomposes as\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Pv+(v-Pv)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwith the first term in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the second in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ker P</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTheir intersection is zero because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P|_W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis the identity. If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u\\in\\ker P</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P\\rho(g)u=\\rho(g)Pu=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso the complement is invariant.</p>", "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dim V=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe decomposition is the empty sum. A nonzero irreducible\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nis already one summand. Otherwise choose a proper nonzero invariant\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsplit it as above, and apply the induction hypothesis to both summands\nof strictly smaller positive dimension. This yields a finite irreducible\ndecomposition.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V=W\\oplus\\ker P</annotation></semantics></math>\nas representations, and every such\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a finite direct sum of irreducibles.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E1/v1 and finite\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dim V</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1. Retain the stated assumptions and\nimport versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Use the equivariant kernel as a complement, then induct on\ndimension.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The recursive decomposition terminates because each proper nonzero\nsummand has smaller dimension.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-2", "source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N2.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 and finite\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dim V</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck: The recursive decomposition terminates because each proper\nnonzero summand has smaller dimension.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-average-a-projection-1\">N1 — Average a projection</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> Choose a vector-space complement by\nextending a basis of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe its projection. Each conjugate of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math>\nlands in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis invariant under every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho(g)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nOn\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w\\in W</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthat conjugate sends\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w</annotation></semantics></math>\nto itself. Thus the average\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math>\nalso maps into\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>\nand is the identity there.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h\\in G</annotation></semantics></math>,\nconjugating\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math>\nby\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho(h)</annotation></semantics></math>\nreplaces the index\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g</annotation></semantics></math>\nby\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">hg</annotation></semantics></math>,\na permutation of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTherefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math>\ncommutes with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho(h)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIts restriction to its image is the identity, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P^2=P</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{im}P=W</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-split-and-terminate-1\">N2 — Split and terminate</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> Every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math>\ndecomposes as\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Pv+(v-Pv)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwith the first term in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the second in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ker P</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTheir intersection is zero because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P|_W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis the identity. If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u\\in\\ker P</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P\\rho(g)u=\\rho(g)Pu=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso the complement is invariant.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dim V=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe decomposition is the empty sum. A nonzero irreducible\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nis already one summand. Otherwise choose a proper nonzero invariant\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsplit it as above, and apply the induction hypothesis to both summands\nof strictly smaller positive dimension. This yields a finite irreducible\ndecomposition.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G=C_2</annotation></semantics></math>\nact on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nby swapping coordinates, with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">char</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{char}k\\ne2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W=k(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nstart with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p(x,y)=(x,x)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nAveraging its two conjugates gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P(x,y)=((x+y)/2,(x+y)/2)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIts kernel is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k(1,-1)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nyielding the trivial and sign summands.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>Over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb F_p</annotation></semantics></math>,\nlet a generator of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_p</annotation></semantics></math>\nact by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T=I+N</annotation></semantics></math>\non a two-dimensional space, where\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N e_2=e_1</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N e_1=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T^p=I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe invariant line\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k e_1</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas no invariant complement: any complementary line has a vector\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_2+a e_1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhose image differs by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_1</annotation></semantics></math>\nand cannot stay in that line. Here\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|G|=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nin the field.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected N1 candidate:</strong> the same average proves\ncomplete reducibility in every characteristic. <strong>Sense:</strong>\nthe unipotent\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_p</annotation></semantics></math>\nexample contradicts the conclusion and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/|G|</annotation></semantics></math>\nis undefined. <strong>Repair:</strong> retain the stated invertibility\nassumption; no averaging repair exists for that counterexample under the\nbroader claim. Recheck the complement and recursive decomposition with\nthe correct field contract.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Use invariant complements to decompose finite-group\nrepresentations before character calculations; this does not itself\nprove the corresponding claim for arbitrary Lie algebras.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a href=\"https://math.mit.edu/~etingof/reprbook.pdf\">Etingof and\ncollaborators, Introduction to Representation Theory</a>, sections on\nrepresentations, characters, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mrow><mi>𝔰</mi><mi>𝔩</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak{sl}_2</annotation></semantics></math>;\n<a\nhref=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-745-lie-groups-and-lie-algebras-i-fall-2020/lists/lecture-notes/\">MIT\nLie Groups and Lie Algebras I lecture notes</a> for solvable Lie\nalgebras.</p>", "sha256": "5792df4d5d41c0dd2f507e82493bbdc2b0ce7a74532fface7a41d5dcbba28239", "pdf": "reports/pdf/maschke-theorem.pdf", "tex": "reports/latex/maschke-theorem.tex", "markdown": "markdown/maschke-theorem.md"}, {"id": "RT-02", "slug": "schur-lemma", "title": "Schur’s Lemma and Scalar Endomorphisms", "level": "Introductory", "idea": "<p>Equivariance turns kernel and image into invariant subspaces.\nAlgebraic closure then produces a scalar that makes an endomorphism\nsingular, forcing it to vanish after subtraction.</p>", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V,W</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe nonzero irreducible representations of a group\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math>\nover a field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>.\nEvery nonzero intertwiner\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T:V\\to W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis an isomorphism. If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>\nis algebraically closed and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nis finite-dimensional, every equivariant endomorphism of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nis scalar. Consequently for finite-dimensional irreducibles over such\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Hom</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dim_k\\operatorname{Hom}_G(V,W)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis one when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>≅</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V\\cong W</annotation></semantics></math>\nand zero otherwise.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Use kernels and images of linear maps, eigenvalue existence for a\nlinear operator on a nonzero finite-dimensional vector space over an\nalgebraically closed field, and linear dimension. The first assertion\ndoes not require finite dimension or algebraic closure.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Control intertwiners by invariant subspaces", "role": "<p>Apply irreducibility separately to the kernel and image.\n<strong>Local obligation:</strong> Every nonzero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math>-intertwiner\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T:V\\to W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis an equivariant isomorphism.</p>", "inputs": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T\\rho_V(g)=\\rho_W(g)T</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand irreducible\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V,W</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p>Every nonzero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math>-intertwiner\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T:V\\to W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis an equivariant isomorphism.</p>", "gate": "<p>Nonzero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math>\nexcludes the full kernel and zero image; check both injectivity and\nsurjectivity.</p>", "repair": "<p>If only injectivity has been shown, use irreducibility of the\ncodomain to establish surjectivity. Withhold this export and recheck its\ndescendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v\\in\\ker T</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T\\rho_V(g)v=\\rho_W(g)Tv=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso the kernel is invariant. The image is invariant because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho_W(g)Tv=T\\rho_V(g)v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Irreducibility gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ker T=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{im}T=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>.\nNonzero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math>\nforces\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ker T=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand image\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a bijective linear map, and multiplying the intertwining equality by\nits inverse shows that the inverse is also equivariant.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation: Every nonzero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math>-intertwiner\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T:V\\to W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis an equivariant isomorphism.</p>", "Memory": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T\\rho_V(g)=\\rho_W(g)T</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand irreducible\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V,W</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Apply irreducibility separately to the kernel and image.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Nonzero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math>\nexcludes the full kernel and zero image; check both injectivity and\nsurjectivity.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Extract scalar endomorphisms", "role": "<p>Subtract an eigenvalue, then apply the nonzero-isomorphism\nalternative. <strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">End</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{End}_G(V)=k\\,\\mathrm{id}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the stated Hom-space dimensions follow.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1 and a finite-dimensional irreducible\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nover algebraically closed\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">End</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{End}_G(V)=k\\,\\mathrm{id}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the stated Hom-space dimensions follow.</p>", "gate": "<p>Eigenvalue existence is precisely where algebraic closure and finite\ndimension enter.</p>", "repair": "<p>If a real irreducible endomorphism is declared scalar, check whether\nit has a real eigenvalue; retain the algebraically closed field for this\nconclusion. Withhold this export and recheck its descendants after a\nversioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">End</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A\\in\\operatorname{End}_G(V)</annotation></semantics></math>\nchoose an eigenvalue\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda\\in k</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A-\\lambda I</annotation></semantics></math>\nis equivariant and has a nonzero kernel. E1 says it cannot be a nonzero\nmap, because then it would be invertible. Therefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=\\lambda I</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>≆</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V\\not\\cong W</annotation></semantics></math>,\nE1 rules out every nonzero intertwiner. If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S:V\\to W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a fixed isomorphism, every intertwiner\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math>\nsatisfies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">End</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S^{-1}T\\in\\operatorname{End}_G(V)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T=\\lambda S</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus the Hom-space is one-dimensional in the isomorphic case.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">End</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{End}_G(V)=k\\,\\mathrm{id}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the stated Hom-space dimensions follow.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E1/v1 and a finite-dimensional irreducible\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nover algebraically closed\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1. Retain the stated assumptions and\nimport versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Subtract an eigenvalue, then apply the nonzero-isomorphism\nalternative.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Eigenvalue existence is precisely where algebraic closure and finite\ndimension enter.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-2", "source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N2.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 and a finite-dimensional irreducible\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nover algebraically closed\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck: Eigenvalue existence is precisely where algebraic closure and\nfinite dimension enter.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-control-intertwiners-by-invariant-subspaces-1\">N1 — Control\nintertwiners by invariant subspaces</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v\\in\\ker T</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T\\rho_V(g)v=\\rho_W(g)Tv=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso the kernel is invariant. The image is invariant because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho_W(g)Tv=T\\rho_V(g)v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> Irreducibility gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ker T=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{im}T=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>.\nNonzero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math>\nforces\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ker T=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand image\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a bijective linear map, and multiplying the intertwining equality by\nits inverse shows that the inverse is also equivariant.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-extract-scalar-endomorphisms-1\">N2 — Extract scalar\nendomorphisms</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">End</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A\\in\\operatorname{End}_G(V)</annotation></semantics></math>\nchoose an eigenvalue\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda\\in k</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A-\\lambda I</annotation></semantics></math>\nis equivariant and has a nonzero kernel. E1 says it cannot be a nonzero\nmap, because then it would be invertible. Therefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=\\lambda I</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>≆</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V\\not\\cong W</annotation></semantics></math>,\nE1 rules out every nonzero intertwiner. If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S:V\\to W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a fixed isomorphism, every intertwiner\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math>\nsatisfies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">End</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S^{-1}T\\in\\operatorname{End}_G(V)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T=\\lambda S</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus the Hom-space is one-dimensional in the isomorphic case.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For the one-dimensional complex characters of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_3</annotation></semantics></math>,\nlet a generator act by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\omega</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nand by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\omega^2</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhere\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\omega^3=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\omega\\ne1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nA linear map is multiplication by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand equivariance gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\omega=\\omega^2a</annotation></semantics></math>,\nhence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nEach character’s endomorphism algebra is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>Over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>,\nlet\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_4</annotation></semantics></math>\nact on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb R^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nby a rotation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J</annotation></semantics></math>\nthrough\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>90</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">90</annotation></semantics></math>\ndegrees. There is no invariant real line, so the representation is\nirreducible. Yet\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J</annotation></semantics></math>\ncommutes with the action and is not a real scalar matrix. The first part\nof Schur’s lemma holds; the scalar conclusion does not.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected N2 export:</strong> every endomorphism of a real\nirreducible representation is scalar. <strong>Sense witness:</strong>\nthe rotation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J</annotation></semantics></math>.\n<strong>Diagnosis:</strong> Memory imported an eigenvalue over a field\nwhere none need exist. <strong>Repair:</strong> apply scalar Schur only\nover the algebraically closed field in §1. The broader real conclusion\nis replaced by the weaker statement that nonzero equivariant\nendomorphisms are invertible. The complex theorem is unchanged.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Use the Hom-space dimension in RT-03 to convert an\naveraging projection into character orthogonality.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a href=\"https://math.mit.edu/~etingof/reprbook.pdf\">Etingof and\ncollaborators, Introduction to Representation Theory</a>, sections on\nrepresentations, characters, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mrow><mi>𝔰</mi><mi>𝔩</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak{sl}_2</annotation></semantics></math>;\n<a\nhref=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-745-lie-groups-and-lie-algebras-i-fall-2020/lists/lecture-notes/\">MIT\nLie Groups and Lie Algebras I lecture notes</a> for solvable Lie\nalgebras.</p>", "sha256": "0e1c7c80814b28b7b079e2d4d7d7fee671306c56540f64a07d04668e2d447265", "pdf": "reports/pdf/schur-lemma.pdf", "tex": "reports/latex/schur-lemma.tex", "markdown": "markdown/schur-lemma.md"}, {"id": "RT-03", "slug": "character-orthogonality", "title": "Orthogonality of Irreducible Characters", "level": "Intermediate", "idea": "<p>Average the group action on the space of all linear maps. Its image\nconsists of intertwiners, and its trace can also be computed from the\ntwo characters.</p>", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe a finite group and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V,W</annotation></semantics></math>\nfinite-dimensional irreducible complex representations. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tr</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\chi_V(g)=\\operatorname{tr}\\rho_V(g)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nprove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mover><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo accent=\"true\">¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|G|^{-1}\\sum_{g\\in G}\\overline{\\chi_V(g)}\\chi_W(g)=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nif\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>≅</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V\\cong W</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0</annotation></semantics></math>\notherwise.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Import RT-02: the complex vector space\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Hom</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Hom}_G(V,W)</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas dimension one or zero in the stated cases. Use finite-dimensional\ntrace, rank of an idempotent, and positive-definite Hermitian forms. An\nidempotent decomposes its space into image and kernel and has trace\nequal to image dimension; this is justified in the proof.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Unitarize and average on Hom", "role": "<p>Average positive forms to compare inverse traces with conjugates, and\naverage the Hom action to project onto invariants. <strong>Local\nobligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>g</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P(A)=|G|^{-1}\\sum_g g\\cdot A</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a projection onto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Hom</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Hom}_G(V,W)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mover><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo accent=\"true\">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\chi_V(g^{-1})=\\overline{\\chi_V(g)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Hom</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>ℂ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathbb C}(V,W)</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g\\cdot A=\\rho_W(g)A\\rho_V(g)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>g</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P(A)=|G|^{-1}\\sum_g g\\cdot A</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a projection onto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Hom</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Hom}_G(V,W)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mover><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo accent=\"true\">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\chi_V(g^{-1})=\\overline{\\chi_V(g)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>Every summand of the averaged form is positive on a nonzero vector;\nfiniteness makes the sum well defined.</p>", "repair": "<p>If an arbitrary initial inner product is assumed invariant, perform\nthe finite-group averaging before identifying inverse and conjugate\ntraces. Withhold this export and recheck its descendants after a\nversioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Start with a positive Hermitian form on each representation and\nreplace it by the sum\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum_g\\langle\\rho(g)v,\\rho(g)w\\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis remains positive definite and is invariant by reindexing. In\northonormal bases every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho(g)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis unitary, so the trace of its inverse is the complex conjugate of its\ntrace.</p>", "<p>The conjugation formula defines a representation on Hom. Reindexing\nthe average shows\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P(A)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis fixed by every group element. A fixed\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math>\nis unchanged by averaging; fixedness is exactly\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A\\rho_V(g)=\\rho_W(g)A</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTherefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P^2=P</annotation></semantics></math>\nand its image is the intertwiner space.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>g</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P(A)=|G|^{-1}\\sum_g g\\cdot A</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a projection onto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Hom</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Hom}_G(V,W)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mover><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo accent=\"true\">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\chi_V(g^{-1})=\\overline{\\chi_V(g)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Hom</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>ℂ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathbb C}(V,W)</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g\\cdot A=\\rho_W(g)A\\rho_V(g)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Average positive forms to compare inverse traces with conjugates, and\naverage the Hom action to project onto invariants.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Every summand of the averaged form is positive on a nonzero vector;\nfiniteness makes the sum well defined.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Compute the trace two ways", "role": "<p>Use a matrix-unit basis to factor the trace of left-right\nmultiplication. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> The normalized\ncharacter inner product equals\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Hom</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dim\\operatorname{Hom}_G(V,W)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand hence the claimed Kronecker value.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1 and the Hom dimension from RT-02. Incoming proof exports: E1/v1\nat N2.1.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p>The normalized character inner product equals\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Hom</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dim\\operatorname{Hom}_G(V,W)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand hence the claimed Kronecker value.</p>", "gate": "<p>Character conjugation belongs on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe representation appearing with an inverse in the Hom action.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the inner product is written without conjugation, restore the\ninverse representation in the Hom action and recompute its trace.\nWithhold this export and recheck its descendants after a versioned\ncorrection.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For matrices\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe diagonal coefficient of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>↦</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A\\mapsto BAC</annotation></semantics></math>\non the matrix unit\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B_{ii}C_{jj}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSumming over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i,j</annotation></semantics></math>\nyields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tr</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>↦</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tr</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tr</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{tr}(A\\mapsto BAC)=\\operatorname{tr}B\\operatorname{tr}C</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tr</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{tr}P=|G|^{-1}\\sum_g\\chi_W(g)\\chi_V(g^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math>\nis idempotent, every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math>\nis the sum\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P(A)+(A-P(A))</annotation></semantics></math>\nfrom image and kernel, with zero intersection. Relative to that\ndecomposition,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas identity and zero blocks, so its trace is the dimension of its\nimage. E1 and RT-02 now give the desired zero or one, and the\ninverse-trace identity gives the stated conjugated formula.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation: The normalized\ncharacter inner product equals\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Hom</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dim\\operatorname{Hom}_G(V,W)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand hence the claimed Kronecker value.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E1/v1 and the Hom dimension from RT-02. Incoming proof exports: E1/v1\nat N2.1. Retain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Use a matrix-unit basis to factor the trace of left-right\nmultiplication.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Character conjugation belongs on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe representation appearing with an inverse in the Hom action.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-2", "source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N2.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 and the Hom dimension from RT-02. Check: Character conjugation\nbelongs on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe representation appearing with an inverse in the Hom action.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-unitarize-and-average-on-hom-1\">N1 — Unitarize and average on\nHom</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> Start with a positive Hermitian form on\neach representation and replace it by the sum\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum_g\\langle\\rho(g)v,\\rho(g)w\\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis remains positive definite and is invariant by reindexing. In\northonormal bases every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho(g)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis unitary, so the trace of its inverse is the complex conjugate of its\ntrace.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> The conjugation formula defines a\nrepresentation on Hom. Reindexing the average shows\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P(A)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis fixed by every group element. A fixed\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math>\nis unchanged by averaging; fixedness is exactly\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A\\rho_V(g)=\\rho_W(g)A</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTherefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P^2=P</annotation></semantics></math>\nand its image is the intertwiner space.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-compute-the-trace-two-ways-1\">N2 — Compute the trace two\nways</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> For matrices\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe diagonal coefficient of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>↦</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A\\mapsto BAC</annotation></semantics></math>\non the matrix unit\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B_{ii}C_{jj}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSumming over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i,j</annotation></semantics></math>\nyields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tr</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>↦</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tr</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tr</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{tr}(A\\mapsto BAC)=\\operatorname{tr}B\\operatorname{tr}C</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tr</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>g</mi></msub><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{tr}P=|G|^{-1}\\sum_g\\chi_W(g)\\chi_V(g^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> Because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math>\nis idempotent, every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math>\nis the sum\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P(A)+(A-P(A))</annotation></semantics></math>\nfrom image and kernel, with zero intersection. Relative to that\ndecomposition,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas identity and zero blocks, so its trace is the dimension of its\nimage. E1 and RT-02 now give the desired zero or one, and the\ninverse-trace identity gives the stated conjugated formula.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_3=\\langle g\\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>,\nlet\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\chi_r(g^j)=\\omega^{rj}</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=0,1,2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe inner product of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\chi_r</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\chi_s</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(1+\\omega^{s-r}+\\omega^{2(s-r)})/3</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIt is one when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=s</annotation></semantics></math>\nand zero otherwise by the geometric sum identity.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>Without complex conjugation, the supposed self-inner-product of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>χ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\chi_1</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_3</annotation></semantics></math>\nwould be\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(1+\\omega^2+\\omega)/3=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nalthough the representation is nonzero irreducible. The conjugation is\nessential.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected N2 calculation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tr</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{tr}(g\\cdot A)=\\chi_V(g)\\chi_W(g)</annotation></semantics></math>.\n<strong>Sense witness:</strong> the zero self-inner-product above.\n<strong>Diagnosis:</strong> Action lost the inverse matrix acting on the\ndomain. <strong>Repair:</strong> retain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho_V(g)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nin the matrix-unit calculation, then use unitarity to conjugate its\ncharacter. The corrected trace proves the original target; recheck the\nfinal orthogonality export.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Derive multiplicities by taking inner products with\nirreducible characters after complete reducibility is established.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a href=\"https://math.mit.edu/~etingof/reprbook.pdf\">Etingof and\ncollaborators, Introduction to Representation Theory</a>, sections on\nrepresentations, characters, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mrow><mi>𝔰</mi><mi>𝔩</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak{sl}_2</annotation></semantics></math>;\n<a\nhref=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-745-lie-groups-and-lie-algebras-i-fall-2020/lists/lecture-notes/\">MIT\nLie Groups and Lie Algebras I lecture notes</a> for solvable Lie\nalgebras.</p>", "sha256": "0eb61116e36fce7a60c5724b0356e427e962330a8f8f693c6799ad061e09be1f", "pdf": "reports/pdf/character-orthogonality.pdf", "tex": "reports/latex/character-orthogonality.tex", "markdown": "markdown/character-orthogonality.md"}, {"id": "RT-04", "slug": "lie-theorem", "title": "Lie’s Theorem for Solvable Complex Lie Algebras", "level": "Advanced", "idea": "<p>An ideal of codimension one provides a weight vector by induction. A\ntrace calculation prevents the remaining direction from changing that\nweight, enabling one last eigenvector selection.</p>", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔤</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak g</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe a finite-dimensional solvable complex Lie algebra and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>𝔤</mi><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi>𝔤</mi><mi>𝔩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho:\\mathfrak g\\to\\mathfrak{gl}(V)</annotation></semantics></math>\na representation on a nonzero finite-dimensional complex vector space.\nThere is a common eigenvector: some\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand linear\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>𝔤</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda:\\mathfrak g\\to\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math>\nsatisfy\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho(y)v=\\lambda(y)v</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y</annotation></semantics></math>.\nConsequently there is a basis in which every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho(y)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis upper triangular. Solvable means the iterated derived series\neventually becomes zero.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Use eigenvalue existence over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntrace of a commutator equal to zero, induction on dimension, and the\nrepresentation identity\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho([x,y])=[\\rho(x),\\rho(y)]</annotation></semantics></math>.\nWrite\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">yv</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho(y)v</annotation></semantics></math>.\nA subalgebra of a solvable algebra is solvable. A nonzero solvable\nalgebra has\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>𝔤</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝔤</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[\\mathfrak g,\\mathfrak g]\\ne\\mathfrak g</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsince equality would make its derived series constant and nonzero.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Choose an ideal weight", "role": "<p>Reduce the Lie algebra dimension, then record the orbit of a weight\nvector under the missing direction. <strong>Local obligation:</strong>\nThere exist\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔤</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔥</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak g=\\mathfrak h\\oplus\\mathbb Cx</annotation></semantics></math>,\na nonzero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand a linear weight\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔥</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">yv_0=\\lambda(y)v_0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Induction on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>𝔤</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d=\\dim\\mathfrak g</annotation></semantics></math>\nand a hyperplane\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔥</mi><mo>⊃</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>𝔤</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak h\\supset[\\mathfrak g,\\mathfrak g]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p>There exist\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔤</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔥</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak g=\\mathfrak h\\oplus\\mathbb Cx</annotation></semantics></math>,\na nonzero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand a linear weight\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔥</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">yv_0=\\lambda(y)v_0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔥</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>\nis an ideal because every bracket with it lies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>𝔤</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[\\mathfrak g,\\mathfrak g]</annotation></semantics></math>;\ninduction decreases algebra dimension.</p>", "repair": "<p>If an arbitrary hyperplane is assumed ideal, choose one containing\nthe derived algebra before applying the commutator calculation. Withhold\nthis export and recheck its descendants after a versioned\ncorrection.</p>", "activities": ["<p>When\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔤</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak g=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nany nonzero vector works. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsolvability makes the derived algebra proper. Choose a hyperplane\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔥</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>\ncontaining it and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\noutside. The hyperplane is an ideal and solvable, of dimension\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Apply the induction hypothesis to the restriction of the\nrepresentation to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔥</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIt gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">yv_0=\\lambda(y)v_0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe scalar function\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\nis linear because the representation is linear and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0</annotation></semantics></math>\nis nonzero.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation: There exist\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔤</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔥</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak g=\\mathfrak h\\oplus\\mathbb Cx</annotation></semantics></math>,\na nonzero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand a linear weight\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔥</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">yv_0=\\lambda(y)v_0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Induction on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>𝔤</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d=\\dim\\mathfrak g</annotation></semantics></math>\nand a hyperplane\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔥</mi><mo>⊃</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>𝔤</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak h\\supset[\\mathfrak g,\\mathfrak g]</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Reduce the Lie algebra dimension, then record the orbit of a weight\nvector under the missing direction.</p>", "Sense": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔥</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>\nis an ideal because every bracket with it lies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>𝔤</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[\\mathfrak g,\\mathfrak g]</annotation></semantics></math>;\ninduction decreases algebra dimension.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Use the trace obstruction", "role": "<p>Triangularize the ideal action on a finite cyclic span and take\ntraces of commutators there. <strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda([x,y])=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1 and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">span</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W=\\operatorname{span}\\{v_0,xv_0,x^2v_0,\\ldots\\}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda([x,y])=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>The finite span\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis invariant under both\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔥</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso restricted commutator traces are legitimate.</p>", "repair": "<p>If a trace is taken on a noninvariant partial span, first pass to the\nfull finite cyclic space\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>\nand establish both invariances. Withhold this export and recheck its\ndescendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Put\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j=x^jv_0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nInduction on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">j</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsimultaneously for every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>,\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">span</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">yv_j-\\lambda(y)v_j\\in\\operatorname{span}(v_0,\\ldots,v_{j-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIndeed\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">yxv_{j-1}=x(yv_{j-1})+[y,x]v_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe first term has the required leading part and the second lies in the\nprevious span because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[y,x]\\in\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the induction hypothesis applies to it.</p>", "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\ge1</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe the first index where\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_m</annotation></semantics></math>\ndepends on its predecessors. It exists by finite dimension. Then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0,\\ldots,v_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nform a basis of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhich is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant\nand, by the preceding formula,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔥</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant.\nFor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>,\nits action on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis triangular with all diagonal entries\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda(y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The action of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[x,y]</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis the commutator of the two restricted operators, so its trace is zero.\nIt also has trace\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\lambda([x,y])</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[x,y]\\in\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCharacteristic zero gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda([x,y])=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda([x,y])=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E1/v1 and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">span</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W=\\operatorname{span}\\{v_0,xv_0,x^2v_0,\\ldots\\}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1. Retain the stated assumptions and\nimport versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Triangularize the ideal action on a finite cyclic span and take\ntraces of commutators there.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The finite span\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis invariant under both\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔥</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso restricted commutator traces are legitimate.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.3 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Preserve the weight space and build a flag", "role": "<p>Use the vanished commutator weights to show\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">xE\\subset E</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen repeat on quotient spaces. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> A\ncommon eigenvector exists, and the representation admits a full\ninvariant flag and upper-triangular matrices.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1 and E2/v1;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>v</mi><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> for all </mtext><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔥</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E=\\{v:yv=\\lambda(y)v\\text{ for all }y\\in\\mathfrak h\\}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N3.1, E2/v1 at N3.1.</p>", "exportId": "E3", "export": "<p>A common eigenvector exists, and the representation admits a full\ninvariant flag and upper-triangular matrices.</p>", "gate": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nsince it contains\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe final induction decreases representation dimension.</p>", "repair": "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E</annotation></semantics></math>\nis claimed invariant without E2, restore the commutator term and use its\nzero weight; otherwise the eigenvector argument is unsupported. Withhold\nthis export and recheck its descendants after a versioned\ncorrection.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v\\in E</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y(xv)=x(yv)+[y,x]v=\\lambda(y)xv+\\lambda([y,x])v=\\lambda(y)xv</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">xE\\subset E</annotation></semantics></math>.\nOn this nonzero finite-dimensional complex space,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas an eigenvector\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔤</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔥</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak g=\\mathfrak h+\\mathbb Cx</annotation></semantics></math>,\nit is a common eigenvector for all of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔤</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak g</annotation></semantics></math>,\ncompleting the induction on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The line\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb Cv</annotation></semantics></math>\nis invariant. To triangularize, induct separately on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dim V</annotation></semantics></math>:\nthe quotient\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V/\\mathbb Cv</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas a representation of the same solvable algebra and a full invariant\nflag by induction. Lift its flag and prepend\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb Cv</annotation></semantics></math>.\nA basis adapted to this flag makes all representing matrices upper\ntriangular.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E3/v1 only after establishing this obligation: A common\neigenvector exists, and the representation admits a full invariant flag\nand upper-triangular matrices.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E1/v1 and E2/v1;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>v</mi><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> for all </mtext><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔥</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E=\\{v:yv=\\lambda(y)v\\text{ for all }y\\in\\mathfrak h\\}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N3.1, E2/v1 at N3.1. Retain the stated\nassumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Use the vanished commutator weights to show\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">xE\\subset E</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen repeat on quotient spaces.</p>", "Sense": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nsince it contains\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe final induction decreases representation dimension.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N3.1–N3.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-2", "source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N2.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">span</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W=\\operatorname{span}\\{v_0,xv_0,x^2v_0,\\ldots\\}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck: The finite span\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis invariant under both\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔥</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso restricted commutator traces are legitimate.</p>"}, {"id": "T1-3", "source": "N1", "target": "N3", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N3.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 and E2/v1;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>v</mi><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> for all </mtext><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔥</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E=\\{v:yv=\\lambda(y)v\\text{ for all }y\\in\\mathfrak h\\}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nsince it contains\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe final induction decreases representation dimension.</p>"}, {"id": "T2-3", "source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "activity": "N3.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 and E2/v1;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>v</mi><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> for all </mtext><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔥</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E=\\{v:yv=\\lambda(y)v\\text{ for all }y\\in\\mathfrak h\\}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nsince it contains\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe final induction decreases representation dimension.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-choose-an-ideal-weight-1\">N1 — Choose an ideal weight</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> When\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔤</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak g=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nany nonzero vector works. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsolvability makes the derived algebra proper. Choose a hyperplane\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔥</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>\ncontaining it and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\noutside. The hyperplane is an ideal and solvable, of dimension\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> Apply the induction hypothesis to the\nrestriction of the representation to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔥</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIt gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">yv_0=\\lambda(y)v_0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe scalar function\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\nis linear because the representation is linear and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0</annotation></semantics></math>\nis nonzero.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-use-the-trace-obstruction-1\">N2 — Use the trace\nobstruction</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> Put\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j=x^jv_0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nInduction on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">j</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsimultaneously for every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>,\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">span</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">yv_j-\\lambda(y)v_j\\in\\operatorname{span}(v_0,\\ldots,v_{j-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIndeed\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">yxv_{j-1}=x(yv_{j-1})+[y,x]v_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe first term has the required leading part and the second lies in the\nprevious span because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[y,x]\\in\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the induction hypothesis applies to it.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\ge1</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe the first index where\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_m</annotation></semantics></math>\ndepends on its predecessors. It exists by finite dimension. Then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0,\\ldots,v_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nform a basis of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhich is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant\nand, by the preceding formula,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔥</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant.\nFor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>,\nits action on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis triangular with all diagonal entries\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda(y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.3.</strong> The action of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[x,y]</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis the commutator of the two restricted operators, so its trace is zero.\nIt also has trace\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\lambda([x,y])</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[x,y]\\in\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCharacteristic zero gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda([x,y])=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-preserve-the-weight-space-and-build-a-flag-1\">N3 — Preserve\nthe weight space and build a flag</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N3.1.</strong> For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v\\in E</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y(xv)=x(yv)+[y,x]v=\\lambda(y)xv+\\lambda([y,x])v=\\lambda(y)xv</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">xE\\subset E</annotation></semantics></math>.\nOn this nonzero finite-dimensional complex space,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas an eigenvector\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔤</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔥</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak g=\\mathfrak h+\\mathbb Cx</annotation></semantics></math>,\nit is a common eigenvector for all of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔤</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak g</annotation></semantics></math>,\ncompleting the induction on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N3.2.</strong> The line\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb Cv</annotation></semantics></math>\nis invariant. To triangularize, induct separately on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dim V</annotation></semantics></math>:\nthe quotient\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V/\\mathbb Cv</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas a representation of the same solvable algebra and a full invariant\nflag by induction. Lift its flag and prepend\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb Cv</annotation></semantics></math>.\nA basis adapted to this flag makes all representing matrices upper\ntriangular.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔤</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak g</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe the upper-triangular\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2\\times2</annotation></semantics></math>\ncomplex matrices acting on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C^2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIts derived algebra consists of strictly upper-triangular matrices,\nwhose mutual brackets vanish, so it is solvable. The vector\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_1</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a common eigenvector with weight\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo minsize=\"120%\" maxsize=\"120%\" stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mi>d</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo minsize=\"120%\" maxsize=\"120%\" stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda\\bigl(\\begin{smallmatrix}a&amp;b\\\\0&amp;d\\end{smallmatrix}\\bigr)=a</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe invariant flag is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⊂</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\subset\\mathbb Ce_1\\subset\\mathbb C^2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>The standard representation of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝔰</mi><mi>𝔩</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak{sl}_2(\\mathbb C)</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas no common eigenvector: the raising matrix kills only\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb Ce_1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhereas the lowering matrix sends\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_1</annotation></semantics></math>\nto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis Lie algebra is not solvable. Over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>,\neven a one-dimensional abelian algebra can act by a rotation without a\nreal eigenvector.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected N3 step:</strong> the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔥</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak h</annotation></semantics></math>-weight\nspace is automatically invariant under\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe identity\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y(xv)=\\lambda(y)xv+\\lambda([y,x])v</annotation></semantics></math>\nexposes the missing term. <strong>Diagnosis:</strong> Intellect omitted\nthe trace obstruction. <strong>Repair:</strong> establish N2 on the\ninvariant cyclic span, then substitute\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda([y,x])=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis fills a genuine logical gap under the original hypotheses; recheck\nthe common eigenvector and flag exports.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Compare this invariant-flag theorem with the\nhighest-weight structure of nonsolvable\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mrow><mi>𝔰</mi><mi>𝔩</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak{sl}_2</annotation></semantics></math>\nin RT-05.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a href=\"https://math.mit.edu/~etingof/reprbook.pdf\">Etingof and\ncollaborators, Introduction to Representation Theory</a>, sections on\nrepresentations, characters, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mrow><mi>𝔰</mi><mi>𝔩</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak{sl}_2</annotation></semantics></math>;\n<a\nhref=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-745-lie-groups-and-lie-algebras-i-fall-2020/lists/lecture-notes/\">MIT\nLie Groups and Lie Algebras I lecture notes</a> for solvable Lie\nalgebras.</p>", "sha256": "20f924b1bceac18694b7af23904877c8958c3db79bd9a538a1ba8addf5257d1b", "pdf": "reports/pdf/lie-theorem.pdf", "tex": "reports/latex/lie-theorem.tex", "markdown": "markdown/lie-theorem.md"}, {"id": "RT-05", "slug": "sl2-irreducible-classification", "title": "Finite-Dimensional Irreducible Representations of sl2", "level": "Advanced", "idea": "<p>Raising must eventually stop because it creates distinct weights.\nLowering from a highest-weight vector then forces the highest weight to\nbe a nonnegative integer.</p>", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝔰</mi><mi>𝔩</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak{sl}_2(\\mathbb C)</annotation></semantics></math>\nhave generators\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e,f,h</annotation></semantics></math>\nsatisfying\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[h,e]=2e</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[h,f]=-2f</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[e,f]=h</annotation></semantics></math>.\nEvery nonzero finite-dimensional irreducible representation is, up to\nisomorphism, exactly one\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor an integer\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIt has basis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0,\\ldots,v_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">hv_j=(n-2j)v_j</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">fv_j=v_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math>\n(and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">fv_n=0</annotation></semantics></math>),\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ev_j=j(n-j+1)v_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\n(and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ev_0=0</annotation></semantics></math>).\nIn particular\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dim V_n=n+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Use eigenvalue existence over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math>,\nlinear independence of eigenvectors for distinct eigenvalues, the\ndisplayed Lie brackets, and polynomial interpolation on finitely many\ndistinct scalars. Irreducibility is assumed for classification; this\nproject does not prove that every finite-dimensional representation is\ncompletely reducible.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Find a highest-weight vector", "role": "<p>Start with an\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>-eigenvector\nand raise it until the last nonzero term. <strong>Local\nobligation:</strong> There is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ev_0=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">hv_0=\\lambda v_0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor some\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda\\in\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>A nonzero finite-dimensional representation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p>There is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ev_0=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">hv_0=\\lambda v_0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor some\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda\\in\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>The raising chain has distinct weights; finite-dimensionality, not a\npreassumed diagonalization of all of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>,\nforces termination.</p>", "repair": "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>\nis declared diagonalizable at the outset, replace that unproved claim by\none eigenvector and the finite raising chain. Withhold this export and\nrecheck its descendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">hw=\\alpha w</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe relation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">he=eh+2e</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(e^jw)=(\\alpha+2j)e^jw</annotation></semantics></math>\nby induction. Nonzero members of this sequence are eigenvectors with\ndistinct eigenvalues and hence linearly independent.</p>", "<p>They cannot all be nonzero in finite dimension. Choose the last\nnonzero one before the first zero, and name it\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIt is killed by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e</annotation></semantics></math>\nand has an\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>-eigenvalue\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>,\nas required.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation: There is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ev_0=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">hv_0=\\lambda v_0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor some\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda\\in\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>A nonzero finite-dimensional representation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Start with an\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>-eigenvector\nand raise it until the last nonzero term.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The raising chain has distinct weights; finite-dimensionality, not a\npreassumed diagonalization of all of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>,\nforces termination.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Quantize the weight and span the module", "role": "<p>Commute\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e</annotation></semantics></math>\nthrough powers of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nand inspect the first vanishing lowered vector. <strong>Local\nobligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda=n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0,\\ldots,v_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nform a basis of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith the stated actions.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1 and irreducibility of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>;\nwrite\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j=f^jv_0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda=n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0,\\ldots,v_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nform a basis of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith the stated actions.</p>", "gate": "<p>The coefficient equation at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_{n+1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nuses\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_n\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand characteristic zero.</p>", "repair": "<p>If termination of lowering is asserted without justification, use the\ndistinct eigenvalues; then apply the formula at the first zero, not\nmerely at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_n</annotation></semantics></math>.\nWithhold this export and recheck its descendants after a versioned\ncorrection.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Inductively,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">hv_j=(\\lambda-2j)v_j</annotation></semantics></math>.\nAlso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ev_0=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ev_{j+1}=efv_j=fev_j+hv_j</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso induction gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ev_j=j(\\lambda-j+1)v_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThese identities use only the brackets and remain true until and\nincluding the first zero vector.</p>", "<p>The nonzero lowered vectors have distinct weights, so finite\ndimension gives a largest\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_n\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_{n+1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nApplying the formula at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n+1</annotation></semantics></math>\nyields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0=(n+1)(\\lambda-n)v_n</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTherefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda=n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The span of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0,\\ldots,v_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nis invariant under\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e,f,h</annotation></semantics></math>\nby these formulas and is nonzero. Irreducibility forces it to equal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>.\nDistinct weights give linear independence, so these vectors are a basis\nand all claimed coefficients follow.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda=n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0,\\ldots,v_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nform a basis of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith the stated actions.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E1/v1 and irreducibility of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>;\nwrite\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j=f^jv_0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1. Retain the stated assumptions and\nimport versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Commute\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e</annotation></semantics></math>\nthrough powers of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nand inspect the first vanishing lowered vector.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The coefficient equation at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_{n+1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nuses\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_n\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand characteristic zero.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.3 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Construct and verify every model", "role": "<p>Check the brackets directly and recover the highest vector from any\nnonzero invariant subspace. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> For each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nexists and is irreducible; these exhaust all isomorphism classes without\nduplication.</p>", "inputs": "<p>An arbitrary integer\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the formulas in the theorem. Incoming proof exports: E2/v1 at\nN3.3.</p>", "exportId": "E3", "export": "<p>For each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nexists and is irreducible; these exhaust all isomorphism classes without\nduplication.</p>", "gate": "<p>Existence and irreducibility of the proposed models must be\nestablished in addition to the classification of a given module.</p>", "repair": "<p>If only the possible highest weights have been listed, add bracket\nverification and the invariant-subspace argument to establish that every\nlisted model really exists and is irreducible. Withhold this export and\nrecheck its descendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Define three linear maps on the abstract basis by the stated\nformulas. The weight differences give\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[h,e]=2e</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[h,f]=-2f</annotation></semantics></math>.\nDirect subtraction gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[e,f]v_j=((j+1)(n-j)-j(n-j+1))v_j=(n-2j)v_j=hv_j</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwith the same result at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">j=0,n</annotation></semantics></math>\nusing zero boundary terms. Thus they define a representation.</p>", "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe a nonzero invariant subspace. A nonzero vector of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas a nonzero component along some\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j</annotation></semantics></math>.\nBecause the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>-eigenvalues\nare distinct, a polynomial in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>\nthat equals one at that weight and zero at the other weights extracts a\nnonzero multiple of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nwithin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math>.\nApplying\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e^j</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives a nonzero multiple of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsince all coefficients\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r(n-r+1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\le r\\le j</annotation></semantics></math>\nare nonzero. Repeated\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nthen yields every basis vector. Hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U=V_n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>N2 identifies any irreducible module with its corresponding model by\nsending the displayed basis to the abstract one. Different\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math>\ngive different dimensions, so the models are pairwise nonisomorphic.\nThis proves existence, uniqueness, and exhaustion.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E3/v1 only after establishing this obligation: For each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nexists and is irreducible; these exhaust all isomorphism classes without\nduplication.</p>", "Memory": "<p>An arbitrary integer\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the formulas in the theorem. Incoming proof exports: E2/v1 at N3.3.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Check the brackets directly and recover the highest vector from any\nnonzero invariant subspace.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Existence and irreducibility of the proposed models must be\nestablished in addition to the classification of a given module.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N3.1–N3.3 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-2", "source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N2.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 and irreducibility of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>;\nwrite\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j=f^jv_0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck: The coefficient equation at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_{n+1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nuses\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_n\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand characteristic zero.</p>"}, {"id": "T2-3", "source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "activity": "N3.3", "gate": "<p>An arbitrary integer\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the formulas in the theorem. Check: Existence and irreducibility of\nthe proposed models must be established in addition to the\nclassification of a given module.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-find-a-highest-weight-vector-1\">N1 — Find a highest-weight\nvector</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> Choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">hw=\\alpha w</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe relation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">he=eh+2e</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(e^jw)=(\\alpha+2j)e^jw</annotation></semantics></math>\nby induction. Nonzero members of this sequence are eigenvectors with\ndistinct eigenvalues and hence linearly independent.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> They cannot all be nonzero in finite\ndimension. Choose the last nonzero one before the first zero, and name\nit\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIt is killed by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e</annotation></semantics></math>\nand has an\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>-eigenvalue\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>,\nas required.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-quantize-the-weight-and-span-the-module-1\">N2 — Quantize the\nweight and span the module</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> Inductively,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">hv_j=(\\lambda-2j)v_j</annotation></semantics></math>.\nAlso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ev_0=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ev_{j+1}=efv_j=fev_j+hv_j</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso induction gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ev_j=j(\\lambda-j+1)v_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThese identities use only the brackets and remain true until and\nincluding the first zero vector.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> The nonzero lowered vectors have distinct\nweights, so finite dimension gives a largest\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_n\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_{n+1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nApplying the formula at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n+1</annotation></semantics></math>\nyields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0=(n+1)(\\lambda-n)v_n</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTherefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda=n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.3.</strong> The span of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0,\\ldots,v_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nis invariant under\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e,f,h</annotation></semantics></math>\nby these formulas and is nonzero. Irreducibility forces it to equal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>.\nDistinct weights give linear independence, so these vectors are a basis\nand all claimed coefficients follow.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-construct-and-verify-every-model-1\">N3 — Construct and verify\nevery model</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N3.1.</strong> Define three linear maps on the abstract\nbasis by the stated formulas. The weight differences give\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[h,e]=2e</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[h,f]=-2f</annotation></semantics></math>.\nDirect subtraction gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[e,f]v_j=((j+1)(n-j)-j(n-j+1))v_j=(n-2j)v_j=hv_j</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwith the same result at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">j=0,n</annotation></semantics></math>\nusing zero boundary terms. Thus they define a representation.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N3.2.</strong> Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe a nonzero invariant subspace. A nonzero vector of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas a nonzero component along some\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j</annotation></semantics></math>.\nBecause the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>-eigenvalues\nare distinct, a polynomial in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>\nthat equals one at that weight and zero at the other weights extracts a\nnonzero multiple of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nwithin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math>.\nApplying\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e^j</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives a nonzero multiple of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsince all coefficients\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r(n-r+1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\le r\\le j</annotation></semantics></math>\nare nonzero. Repeated\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nthen yields every basis vector. Hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U=V_n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N3.3.</strong> N2 identifies any irreducible module with\nits corresponding model by sending the displayed basis to the abstract\none. Different\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math>\ngive different dimensions, so the models are pairwise nonisomorphic.\nThis proves existence, uniqueness, and exhaustion.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=2</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe weights are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2,0,-2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe lowering chain is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>↦</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>↦</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>↦</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0\\mapsto v_1\\mapsto v_2\\mapsto0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ev_1=2v_0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ev_2=2v_1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nAt the middle vector,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">efv_1=2v_1</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">fev_1=2v_1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso their difference equals\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">hv_1=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nAt\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe difference is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2v_0=hv_0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>Irreducibility is essential for the conclusion that one chain spans\nthe entire module. The direct sum\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_0\\oplus V_0</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas dimension two but\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=e=f=0</annotation></semantics></math>;\nit is not the irreducible\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>\nweights are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1,-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected N2 conclusion:</strong> a highest-weight chain spans\nevery finite-dimensional representation. <strong>Sense witness:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_0\\oplus V_0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhere any generated chain is just one line. <strong>Diagnosis:</strong>\nthe passage from a nonzero invariant span to all of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>\nsilently used irreducibility. <strong>Repair:</strong> invoke the stated\nirreducibility hypothesis precisely at N2.3. No general\ncomplete-reducibility claim is added; recheck the basis and dimension\nexports.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Develop the separate complete-reducibility theorem\nand then tensor-product decomposition rules, keeping them distinct from\nthis irreducible classification.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a href=\"https://math.mit.edu/~etingof/reprbook.pdf\">Etingof and\ncollaborators, Introduction to Representation Theory</a>, sections on\nrepresentations, characters, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mrow><mi>𝔰</mi><mi>𝔩</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak{sl}_2</annotation></semantics></math>;\n<a\nhref=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-745-lie-groups-and-lie-algebras-i-fall-2020/lists/lecture-notes/\">MIT\nLie Groups and Lie Algebras I lecture notes</a> for solvable Lie\nalgebras.</p>", "sha256": "84b227c65c57acbd724a4b763c22a704d6811338a66b6b1565f10aa687803625", "pdf": "reports/pdf/sl2-irreducible-classification.pdf", "tex": "reports/latex/sl2-irreducible-classification.tex", "markdown": "markdown/sl2-irreducible-classification.md"}], "links": [{"source": "RT-02", "target": "RT-03", "label": "Schur’s Lemma and Scalar Endomorphisms", "detail": "RT-03 explicitly imports RT-02 under the version and assumptions in its import contract."}], "evidence": "Authored proof walkthroughs relative to declared imports; no agent execution or formal verification claimed."};
